WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.366 --> 00:00:00.966
One-to-one

2
00:00:00.966 --> 00:00:04.186
English lessons can go in wildly different directions.

3
00:00:04.406 --> 00:00:06.700
One learner is collecting every animal idiom

4
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.826
they can find.

5
00:00:07.846 --> 00:00:10.866
Another wants to finally crack the present perfect.

6
00:00:11.086 --> 00:00:13.206
A new student is moving to Sydney to study

7
00:00:13.206 --> 00:00:14.306
marine biology,

8
00:00:14.366 --> 00:00:17.126
and suddenly you're deep into whale song dialects,

9
00:00:17.126 --> 00:00:19.386
satellite tags, and Australian slang.

10
00:00:19.606 --> 00:00:20.406
And sometimes,

11
00:00:20.406 --> 00:00:23.546
you just opened your laptop at a rooftop hostel in Rio,

12
00:00:23.566 --> 00:00:24.900
and you've only got three minutes

13
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.133
before the next lesson.

14
00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:29.046
Atlas lets you turn any of those starting points

15
00:00:29.046 --> 00:00:31.366
into rich, specific teaching material

16
00:00:31.366 --> 00:00:33.126
built around the learner in front of you

17
00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:33.966
in seconds.

18
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.646
Create from their work, a language target,

19
00:00:36.646 --> 00:00:39.486
a sudden question, something Atlas suggests,

20
00:00:39.486 --> 00:00:42.146
or any offbeat idea you wanna explore together.

21
00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:44.146
Shape it around the way you teach.

22
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:46.366
Then explore it together through questions,

23
00:00:46.366 --> 00:00:47.886
stories, context,

24
00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:50.386
different perspectives, and real conversation.

25
00:00:50.606 --> 00:00:52.666
And next week, you're not starting over.

26
00:00:52.686 --> 00:00:55.046
That expression you stopped to work on last Tuesday

27
00:00:55.046 --> 00:00:58.166
is still there, along with all the material you created,

28
00:00:58.166 --> 00:00:59.406
what you've learnt about them,

29
00:00:59.406 --> 00:01:01.066
and the progress you've made together.

30
00:01:01.206 --> 00:01:03.406
Bring back a subject you explored months ago,

31
00:01:03.406 --> 00:01:04.926
or get creative with whatever

32
00:01:04.926 --> 00:01:06.586
new thing they bring into the lesson.

33
00:01:06.726 --> 00:01:08.646
When the material matters to the learner,

34
00:01:08.646 --> 00:01:10.166
the conversation goes further,

35
00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:11.233
and so does the teaching.

36
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:12.346
Atlas.
